1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Five classes, stacked. Each is a proper subset of the one above it.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Type 3 to Type 0: what changes is only the shape a rule is allowed to have.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,500
REC is not one of Chomsky's four types. It sits between Type 1 and Type 0.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,000
Read the chain upwards: a bigger class is a machine with more memory.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Type 3 buys a finite automaton: a fixed number of states and no memory.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Type 2 buys a stack: one comparison can be remembered, and only one.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,500
Type 1 buys a tape no longer than the input. That ceiling is what makes it decidable.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Type 0 buys an unbounded tape, and with it the halting problem.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
The regular pumping lemma, run as a search rather than recited as a proof.

10
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,000
At p = 1 there is 1 split, at p = 8 there are 36. Every split pumps a's into b's.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,500
Survivors: zero, at every pumping length from 1 to 8.

12
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:30,000
So a^n b^n is in CFL and not in REG: one strict link, proved by search.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,500
Seven rules, and not one of them shrinks its sentential form.

14
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:45,000
The derivation sorts the B's and C's, then converts them one at a time.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,500
A bounded search finds exactly three terminal strings up to length 11.

16
00:01:52,500 --> 00:02:00,000
So a^n b^n c^n is context-sensitive and not context-free.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,500
CSL is NSPACE(n). Savitch puts it inside SPACE(n^2).

18
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:15,000
The space hierarchy theorem says SPACE(n^2) is a proper subset of SPACE(n^3).

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,500
Take a language in SPACE(n^3) but not SPACE(n^2): decidable, and not context-sensitive.

20
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:30,000
a^n b^n c^n needs two counters, and a linear tape holds them. A 2^n-cell language cannot fit.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,500
RE is the class with a machine that says yes. It may say nothing else.

22
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:45,000
REC is the class with a machine that always halts, and it is closed under complement.

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,500
Post: a set is recursive exactly when it and its complement are both r.e.

24
00:02:52,500 --> 00:03:00,000
The halting set is in RE and not in REC, and its complement is in neither.

25
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,500
Every class here is closed under union, concatenation, star, reversal and with a regular set.

26
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:15,000
Three cells fail: CFL twice and RE once.

27
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:22,500
Two of the failures are one fact: no complement means no intersection.

28
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:30,000
The third is Post: RE without complement is REC.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:37,500
L1 pairs equal a's with b's. L2 pairs equal b's with c's. Both are context-free.

30
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:45,000
On i, j, k from 0 to 4: 125 strings, 25 in L1, 25 in L2, 45 in the union.

31
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:52,500
The intersection has 5 strings, and they are exactly a^n b^n c^n.

32
00:03:52,500 --> 00:04:00,000
Scene 3 already broke that language with the context-free pumping lemma.

33
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,500
Regular languages answer all five questions. So do recursive languages.

34
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:15,000
Context-free and context-sensitive languages answer three of the five.

35
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,500
Decidability does not fall as the class grows: REC decides more than CSL.

36
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:30,000
For r.e. languages only membership is semi-decidable. Everything else is lost.

37
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:37,500
Four questions in order: DFA, CFG, monotonic grammar, always-halting machine.

38
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:45,000
Then ask the two questions that separate the rungs you cannot see.

39
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:52,500
Trap one: not regular does not mean context-free.

40
00:04:52,500 --> 00:05:00,000
Name the class by the machine, never by the look of the strings.

